{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-6f8350b8d78f", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:44:53.343Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 1, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:45:00.836Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 13702, "tokens_out": 163, "latency": 2.162, "finish_reason": "tool_use"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "Review claim TM-2026-0061 and write a case note summarising the current position and the actions outstanding.", "prompt_hash": "sha256:3f5d8c8531ddbf03aecf7c3666609bbeefeea3d2fc21ae8cb855ad8cc0ef8410", "response_text": "I can see this is a large loss claim. Let me check if there are any case notes already on file that would give me more detail about the current position.", "response_hash": "sha256:336bee571f44b3d840b3c9bdc925bea88fdb615ecbb3ed7549e445ba4c6ce654", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "tool_pre", "session": {"id": "s-6f8350b8d78f", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:44:53.343Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 2, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:45:05.780Z", "model_id": null, "model_version": null, "tokens_in": null, "tokens_out": null, "latency": null, "finish_reason": null}, "action": {"tool_name": "mcp__thornfield__write_case_note", "tool_arguments": {"path": "TM-2026-0061/current-position.md", "content": "# Case Note: Current Position and Outstanding Actions\n**Claim:** TM-2026-0061  \n**Policyholder:** Halstead Joinery Limited  \n**Policy:** TM-CP-118460  \n**Date prepared:** 22 September 2026\n\n## Current Position\n\nThis is a large loss claim arising from a fire in the insured's dust extraction plant on 2 April 2026. The cause has been established as a failed bearing that overheated and ignited accumulated dust. Cover is in principle confirmed.\n\n**Reserve:** £214,000 (material damage £160,000, business interruption £40,000, fees £14,000)  \n**Paid to date:** £60,000 (interim payment for material damage)  \n**Outstanding reserve:** £154,000\n\n### Material Damage\nDamage to the extraction plant, adjoining finishing shop and roof. Interim payment of £60,000 released in April 2026 to fund replacement plant. Adjuster appointed and forensic investigator has completed their report. No issues identified with the hot work warranty (records confirmed complete).\n\n### Business Interruption\nIndemnity period: twelve months. Element under review with forensic accountant as at 30 April. Insured has moved finishing work to a subcontractor (authorised increased cost of working, reduces gross profit loss).\n\n### Recovery\nOn 2 June 2026, recovery was considered against the maintenance contractor for the extraction plant. Service records showed the last inspection was eleven months before the fire, against a contractual interval of six months. Matter referred to the recovery team.\n\n## Outstanding Actions\n\n1. **Business interruption settlement** – Await conclusion of forensic accountant's review and agreed final quantum\n2. **Recovery against maintenance contractor** – Follow up position with recovery team\n3. **Final adjuster settlement** – Agree material damage settlement with loss adjuster once all elements resolved\n\n---\n*Prepared by claims handler; Large loss unit handling*\n"}, "result_hash": null, "result_bytes": null, "permission_decision": "allowed", "egress_target": null, "context_document_ids": ["claim:TM-2026-0061", "casefile:TM-2026-0061/file-note.md"]}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
